(6433588, 934873, 103142, '<td valign="top">This is a wonderful capture, but I do think the noise did you in.<br/> <br/>Regarding noise -- I think Photoshop is lousy at denoising. Have you tried topaz denoise? I think it''s absolutely wonderful and I highly recommend it.<br/> <br/>(I gave it an 8, btw.)</td>', 'This is a wonderful capture, but I do think the noise did you in. Regarding noise -- I think Photoshop is lousy at denoising. Have you tried topaz denoise? I think it''s absolutely wonderful and I highly recommend it. (I gave it an 8, btw.)', '2011-06-03 23:22:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(6477659, 935695, 12611, '<td valign="top">Love the cat the salmon walls and the glass; this is a very interesting composition, you have a great eye, and a terrific sense of harmony and balance without symmetry.</td>', 'Love the cat the salmon walls and the glass; this is a very interesting composition, you have a great eye, and a terrific sense of harmony and balance without symmetry.', '2011-07-21 11:30:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6499574, 935259, 76335, '<td valign="top">No Comment Chicken Soup<br/> <br/>2 Tbsp butter<br/>1 small onion, finely chopped<br/>3 medium carrots, thinly sliced<br/>3 medium parsnips, peeled and sliced<br/>1 medium leek, sliced<br/>7 cups chicken broth<br/>1 cup uncooked orzo pasta<br/>2 cups shredded cooked chicken breast<br/>2 Tbsp chopped fresh dill weed<br/>1/2 tsp salt<br/> <br/>Melt butter in Dutch oven over medium heat. Cook onions, carrots, parsnips, leek in butter, stirring occasionally until carrots are tender. Stir in broth and pasta. Heat to boiling and reduce heat to low. Cover and simmer 15 minutes, stirring occasionally until pasta is tender. Stir in remaining ingredients. Cover and simmer 5 minutes or until hot. <br/> <br/>I guess Campbells beat General Mills in the soup race?</td>', 'No Comment Chicken Soup 2 Tbsp butter1 small onion, finely chopped3 medium carrots, thinly sliced3 medium parsnips, peeled and sliced1 medium leek, sliced7 cups chicken broth1 cup uncooked orzo pasta2 cups shredded cooked chicken breast2 Tbsp chopped fresh dill weed1/2 tsp salt Melt butter in Dutch oven over medium heat. Cook onions, carrots, parsnips, leek in butter, stirring occasionally until carrots are tender. Stir in broth and pasta. Heat to boiling and reduce heat to low. Cover and simmer 15 minutes, stirring occasionally until pasta is tender. Stir in remaining ingredients. Cover and simmer 5 minutes or until hot.  I guess Campbells beat General Mills in the soup race?', '2011-08-09 17:56:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(6504704, 935417, 12611, '<td valign="top">I thought it was sand until I read the comment below and saw the edge- great feeling of time and decay in this shot.</td>', 'I thought it was sand until I read the comment below and saw the edge- great feeling of time and decay in this shot.', '2011-08-15 09:20:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(6628845, 934669, 91783, '<td valign="top">I think this is a great photo, although i think that the PP is just a little sloppy. It could have been a little cleaner around her body. But besides that the colors and clearity are really good! really nice DOF!<br/> <br/>Congrats on finish!</td>', 'I think this is a great photo, although i think that the PP is just a little sloppy. It could have been a little cleaner around her body. But besides that the colors and clearity are really good! really nice DOF! Congrats on finish!', '2011-12-30 16:14:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6635334, 935202, 3936, '<td valign="top">This image is right at being over exposed.  The highlights on the chest are at the point of burnout, and losing detail.  As this is an advanced editing challenge, the bruise or mark on the skin below the arm, and just above the dress, should be edited out.  The image also looks a bit over sharpened as there is a clumping effect in the bokeh of the background.  Lighting and colors are well done, a relatively shalow depth of field was used well to isolate the subject from a busy background.  Overall a good phot and pose.  As evidenced by your above average score.</td>', 'This image is right at being over exposed.  The highlights on the chest are at the point of burnout, and losing detail.  As this is an advanced editing challenge, the bruise or mark on the skin below the arm, and just above the dress, should be edited out.  The image also looks a bit over sharpened as there is a clumping effect in the bokeh of the background.  Lighting and colors are well done, a relatively shalow depth of field was used well to isolate the subject from a busy background.  Overall a good phot and pose.  As evidenced by your above average score.', '2012-01-04 23:30:01.000000', NULL, 0),
